WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Heating systems keep people alive in winter. You need to know them cold.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
A heat pump is an AC that runs in reverse. A reversing valve switches
refrigerant flow direction. In cooling mode the outdoor coil rejects heat. In
heating mode the outdoor coil absorbs heat from outdoor air. The O wire

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Reversing Valve: A 4-way valve changing refrigerant flow direction between
heating and cooling.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Defrost Cycle: Temporarily switches to cooling to melt outdoor coil ice.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Heat pumps are the fastest-growing
residential HVAC segment.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Know O vs B convention before diagnosing. And — Stuck
reversing valve causes heating in cooling mode or vice versa

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

